# fixedbugs, defect 022, panel 122, 2026-09-09.
#
# SYMPTOM: `heroes check` silent, `heroes build` wrote the binary, and reading
# the field under `--sanitize` reports `AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free`,
# READ of size 7.
#
# CAUSE: `selfhost/emit/gate.hero` refused `cstr` as the element of an array, a
# map and a `T?`, and a record FIELD was the hole. Worse, that refusal's own
# note prescribed this shape: *"hold the pointer in a `record` and make an
# array of that instead"*. The emitter was sending readers through the one
# door nobody had shut.
#
# FIX: panel 122 R4, and the note was rewritten in the same commit. A group's
# `record` may still hold a `cstr` — there the fields are the header's and C
# owns the bytes, which § FFI states — so the clause is scoped to records
# outside a group. Measured free: no such field existed in this tree.

extern "string.h"
    function strlen(s: cstr) -> u64

record Holder
    c: cstr  #~ cstr_in_a_record

function held(n: i64) -> Holder
    return Holder(c: ("heap-" + n.to_str()).cstr())

function main()
    print(strlen(s: held(n: 7).c).to_str())
